{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
There was a [F]wedding in Cana [C]town
The music [Dm]playing all a[Bb]round
But the [F]wine ran out before the [C]night
And Mary [Dm]said, they have no more [Bb]wine
Do what[F]ever he tells you, do what[C]ever he says
[Dm]Fill the jars with wa[Bb]ter, fill them to the brim
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Oh, the [F]best wine is [C]now
He [Dm]kept the best for [Bb]now
Water into [F]wine, his glory [C]shine [Dm]
