{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Six stone jars along the [C]wall
[Dm]The servants filled them one and [Bb]all
[F]Draw it out and take it to the [C]master of the feast
[Dm]He tasted and he said, [Bb]you kept the best wine [F]for [C]last
Everybody [Dm]serves the good wine [Bb]first
[F]But you kept the good wine un[C]til now [Bb]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Oh, the [F]best wine is [C]now
He [Dm]kept the best for [Bb]now
